    {
      "id": "529c5a75-6021-467d-8741-9d9e0dca7e95",
      "name": "Why MCP is awesome: one protocol, every tool",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Why MCP is awesome: one protocol, every tool",
      "docTypeId": "7189041a-69ca-47ff-892a-e367366eb4a5",
      "templateId": "ee187aa9-feed-41aa-8877-8f2041acc9a2",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "excerpt",
          "value": "The Model Context Protocol gives AI agents one standard way to talk to every tool they need. Here is why that changes how we build content sites."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "featuredImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "2c7b4fe3-ae88-43e9-81af-6e0ac7972e2a",
              "mediaKey": "7ae9edf2-4e75-4962-8b07-f5f2a9d4b48f",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.DateTime",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "publishedDate",
          "value": "2026-10-07 00:00:00"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "body",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "f2639f8d-e13c-4e67-b06b-e8ae5c25046d",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "57428c1e-3bd8-4aa0-8154-e9b2712a41bd",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "2c880ac6-96a8-4cbe-af3f-ffd56965112c",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "15e609df-c03c-48f3-85ae-d8a9055fd591",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "976f9ffb-9d9b-40b0-9730-64dd9ddc830c",
                "key": "f2639f8d-e13c-4e67-b06b-e8ae5c25046d",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "body",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>If you have ever wired an AI assistant up to a handful of internal tools, you know the pain: every integration is a bespoke adapter, every schema is a snowflake, and the moment you add tool number six the whole thing starts to creak.</p><p>The Model Context Protocol (MCP) fixes this by standardising the conversation. One protocol, one discovery mechanism, one way to call a tool — no matter what the tool does or who built it.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "2130109b-aa66-44b2-b932-b19b0d045d73",
                "key": "57428c1e-3bd8-4aa0-8154-e9b2712a41bd",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "quote",
                    "value": "MCP is the USB-C of AI tooling: one connector, and everything just plugs in."
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "attribution",
                    "value": "The case for a universal tool protocol"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "3406fa98-72a3-4298-b06b-497c4d882f28",
                "key": "2c880ac6-96a8-4cbe-af3f-ffd56965112c",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "f83653ed-bd04-494a-8740-0394320e8179",
                        "mediaKey": "a7392cd5-b43a-483d-94e1-8dfa3fadfd8e",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "Cables that all speak the same protocol — photo by Hal Gatewood on Unsplash"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "976f9ffb-9d9b-40b0-9730-64dd9ddc830c",
                "key": "15e609df-c03c-48f3-85ae-d8a9055fd591",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "body",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>For a content site like this one, the practical win is speed and consistency. The same server that reads the content tree writes to it — creating the schema, uploading the media and publishing the pages through one authenticated, versioned API.</p><p>No screen-scraping the backoffice. No brittle import scripts. Just a clean contract between the model and the CMS.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "f2639f8d-e13c-4e67-b06b-e8ae5c25046d",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "57428c1e-3bd8-4aa0-8154-e9b2712a41bd",
                "culture": null,
