    {
      "id": "a7d2f45c-c8fa-4be8-8b74-63b41ab8dcbd",
      "name": "Why MCP is awesome: content at the speed of thought",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Why MCP is awesome: content at the speed of thought",
      "docTypeId": "7189041a-69ca-47ff-892a-e367366eb4a5",
      "templateId": "ee187aa9-feed-41aa-8877-8f2041acc9a2",
      "state": "PublishedPendingChanges",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "excerpt",
          "value": "From an empty database to a published blog in one sitting. A look at what happens when your CMS speaks MCP."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "featuredImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "3fafa912-3d76-4b3d-9d87-8a7d29308175",
              "mediaKey": "7947d22c-5847-43aa-a9f8-b31f40b9b96c",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.DateTime",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "publishedDate",
          "value": "2026-10-09 00:00:00"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "body",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "68215221-7633-451c-be10-ff14c8be5111",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "0f1fcf8f-3ee5-4f3e-b7f0-b1cb6c52ceb7",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "1fbaa504-f0ce-433f-8c13-59b73a24576e",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "80e21fa5-2f4c-431d-889d-802ab11263ae",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "976f9ffb-9d9b-40b0-9730-64dd9ddc830c",
                "key": "68215221-7633-451c-be10-ff14c8be5111",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "body",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>This entire blog — the schema, the pages, the images, the publishing — was created by an AI agent talking to Umbraco over the Model Context Protocol. No human clicked a single button in the backoffice.</p><p>That is the headline, but the interesting part is what it felt like: modeling content, writing posts and shipping them became one continuous conversation instead of three separate tools glued together with copy-paste.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "3406fa98-72a3-4298-b06b-497c4d882f28",
                "key": "0f1fcf8f-3ee5-4f3e-b7f0-b1cb6c52ceb7",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "c444b5e3-5884-4c5e-b148-dc1f2db15ea1",
                        "mediaKey": "8f1c0f11-7f95-4cd1-95cf-0bbc51015bcd",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "A circuit board with standardised connections — photo by Alexandre Debiève on Unsplash"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "976f9ffb-9d9b-40b0-9730-64dd9ddc830c",
                "key": "1fbaa504-f0ce-433f-8c13-59b73a24576e",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "body",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>MCP turns the CMS into a first-class citizen of the agent's world. The agent can discover what content types exist, understand their properties, and then act with confidence — creating, updating and publishing through the same management API the backoffice uses.</p><p>The result is a workflow where the distance between an idea and a published page is measured in sentences, not in tickets.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "2130109b-aa66-44b2-b932-b19b0d045d73",
                "key": "80e21fa5-2f4c-431d-889d-802ab11263ae",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "quote",
                    "value": "The best tool interface is the one the model already knows how to use."
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "attribution",
                    "value": "Why MCP wins for content operations"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "68215221-7633-451c-be10-ff14c8be5111",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
